  "Many students believe that homework helps them learn, but the amount they receive can become overwhelming. When teachers assign several hours of work each night, students often have less time for sleep, exercise, and family. Some research suggests that moderate homework improves test scores, while too much can increase stress. Schools should therefore find a balance that supports learning without harming students' health. One possible solution is to coordinate assignments across classes so that major projects are not due on the same day. This approach would help students manage their time and still practice the skills they need.";

